This plugin vendors two skills from Lauren Tan's "pstack" plugin, shipped in Cursor's
official plugin repo:

    https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack

    pstack/skills/unslop/SKILL.md            -> skills/unslop/SKILL.md
    pstack/skills/technical-writing/SKILL.md -> skills/technical-writing/SKILL.md

Upstream commit:

    f5bdd6826fd0a0d9cbc4347134c3a74a200b9d9d

SKILL.md is the whole of each skill upstream. The rest of pstack is a Cursor-oriented
plugin and is deliberately not vendored. The two skills share one plugin and one pin
because technical-writing cites unslop's rule ids, and two pins could drift apart. The
upstream repo root carries no licence file; `pstack/LICENSE` is MIT, covers both files, and
is reproduced below.

LOCAL MODIFICATIONS
-------------------

Both SKILL.md files are NOT verbatim. Three patches apply on top of upstream, in this order:

    patches/0001-narrow-the-invocation-gate.patch
        Drops `disable-model-invocation: true` from technical-writing and narrows its
        description, so the model reaches for it on prose a reader comes back to and not
        on a bare commit subject or chat.
    patches/0002-repo-specifics.patch
        Fixes two technical-writing lines that describe pstack's repo: code indentation
        now follows the file, and a change to unslop goes to patches/ in this directory.
    patches/0003-allow-model-invocation-of-unslop.patch
        Drops `disable-model-invocation: true` from unslop, so the model can invoke it.
        The body stays byte-for-byte upstream.

Two files are local additions, not patches:

    skills/unslop/agents/openai.yaml
    skills/technical-writing/agents/openai.yaml

Upstream ships no openai.yaml. Each sets `policy.allow_implicit_invocation`, the Codex half
of 0001 and 0003. A re-sync copies SKILL.md only and leaves them alone.

RE-SYNCING
----------

    1. Copy pstack/skills/unslop/SKILL.md over skills/unslop/SKILL.md
    2. Copy pstack/skills/technical-writing/SKILL.md over
       skills/technical-writing/SKILL.md
    3. git apply patches/0001-narrow-the-invocation-gate.patch
    4. git apply patches/0002-repo-specifics.patch
    5. git apply patches/0003-allow-model-invocation-of-unslop.patch
    6. Update the commit SHA above; regenerate any patch that stops applying

The patches are ordinary `git diff` output with `a/plugins/unslop/skills/...` paths,
so apply them from the repo root. To regenerate one, commit the state it applies to,
redo the change on top of that, and `git diff` the two commits. Verify the chain by
applying it to a fresh upstream copy in a scratch directory and diffing the result
against skills/. The two SKILL.md files must be byte-identical; the agents/ directories
exist only on this side.

